  "summary_en": "Nevada Revised Statutes Chapter 482A regulates testing and operation of autonomous vehicles on state highways. It defines automation levels via SAE J3016, requires $5 million insurance or bond for testing, human operator requirements, minimal risk condition for fully autonomous vehicles, crash reporting, state preemption of local rules, and penalties.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing requires $5,000,000 insurance, self-insurance, or bond.",
   "Human operator must be able to take control, except fully autonomous vehicles meeting minimal risk condition requirements.",
   "Crashes during testing with injury or damage over $750 must be reported within 10 business days.",
   "Only the Department may regulate AV technology; local governments cannot tax or impose requirements.",
   "Manufacturers not liable for defects from third-party conversion or modification; fines up to $2,500."
  ],
